# operror.ti59 Op 01 error in emulator (FIXED)
#
# Expections: - Calc. display shows 1731371735
# Reality:    - Calc. display shows 1731371734

# The display changes during Op 01 (correct before, wrong after).
# Op 01 stores the wrong value. This only hgappens when the value is retrieved from
# a memory register (RCL). When the same number is keyed in, Op 01 does not change
# it when storing.
# Real hardware does not show this behaviour.
#
# Root cause: not Op 01 itself. The REGISTERS: preset loader
# (encodeTI59BCD in App/StateFileLoader.swift) converted the decimal literal
# to BCD via an iterative float digit-extraction loop (mantissa/pow, then
# repeated subtract+multiply-by-10). That loop accumulates floating-point
# rounding error across the 13 mantissa digits, so register 15 was actually
# stored as 1731371734.999090, not 1731371735. IDLE's normal display
# formatting rounds this back to ...735, hiding the error, but Op 01's
# processing exposed the true stored value as ...734. Keying the digits in
# directly builds the BCD register digit-by-digit with no floating-point
# step, so it never hit this. Fixed by using a correctly-rounded %.12e
# string conversion instead of the manual loop.

#MODEL: TI-59

REGISTERS:
15 = 1731371735

KEYSTROKES:
Trace: operror.bin
43  RCL
82  1
73  5
21  2nd
64  Op
